      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ and the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B$ are given below. What is $[x]_{C}?$ \n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Given the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
